Figure 6 illustrates Nano-11's ability to improve antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells in the draining lymph node and increase antigen retention at the injection site. Panel **a** shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) exhibit the highest expression of the costimulatory molecule CD86 compared to lymphoid tissue resident DCs (LTDCs) and monocytes/macrophages (Mo/MΦ). Panel **b** phenotyping of OVA-positive MigDCs further reveals the distribution of antigen within different dendritic cell subsets. Panel **c** demonstrates in vivo that Nano-11, similar to aluminum hydroxide, significantly increases the retention of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled OVA at the injection site over time, compared to soluble OVA which clears rapidly.